<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 5 March, from 363 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/persia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/persia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/363">363 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,663 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Julian sets out to invade Persia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Julian left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> with a large army to attack the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. He reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ctesiphon">Ctesiphon</a> but was killed during the retreat in June, and with him ended the last attempt to restore paganism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ctesiphon">Ctesiphon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1046">1046 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">980 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nasir Khusraw sets out on his seven-year journey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Persian poet and philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-khusraw">Nasir Khusraw</a> set out on a pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, taking an indirect route north toward the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. His account of the seven-year journey, the Safarnama, described the wealth of Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-khusraw">Nasir Khusraw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1279">1279 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">747 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lithuania defeats the Livonian Order at Aizkraukle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Aizkraukle in present-day Latvia, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/traidenis">Traidenis</a> defeated the Livonian branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, killing 71 knights, including the grand master, Ernst von Rassburg. Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nameisis">Nameisis</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semigallians">Semigallians</a> then recognised Traidenis as suzerain.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1496">1496 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">530 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VII commissions John Cabot to seek new lands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Letters patent authorised the Venetian navigator to sail under the English flag in search of unknown lands. His 1497 voyage reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and later underpinned English claims there.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1770">1770 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">256 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British soldiers kill five in the Boston Massacre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soldiers fired into a crowd taunting them in King Street, killing five men, including Crispus Attucks. Paul Revere's engraving of the scene became powerful propaganda against British rule.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1946">1946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill warns of an 'iron curtain' across Europe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking at Fulton, Missouri, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> declared that an iron curtain had descended across the continent from the Baltic to the Adriatic. The speech popularised the phrase and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> divide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joseph Stalin dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet dictator died four days after a stroke at his dacha near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. His rule had brought rapid industrialisation and victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, but also famine, purges and millions of deaths.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alberto Korda photographs Che Guevara</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a> memorial for victims of a ship explosion, Korda captured Guevara's gaze in a photograph later titled 'Guerrillero Heroico'. It became one of the most reproduced images in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty enters into force</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The treaty committed nuclear powers not to spread weapons and others not to acquire them, while promoting peaceful nuclear energy. With 191 parties, it is the most widely joined arms control agreement.</p></div></li></ol>
